  "lineage": "New Caledonian Kanak popular music codified in the mid-1980s around the independence movement, with bands Bwanjep, Gurejele and Edou fusing customary pilou dance rhythm and bwanjep bamboo-stamping patterns with Jamaican reggae backbeat — mid-tempo 4/4 around 80-100 BPM, one-drop or half-time kit under offbeat guitar chops, electric bass carrying the melodic weight, unison male choruses in Drehu, Paicî and French, lyrics on land, custom and independence.",
